From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:21:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: keep VCN33 (CONN rail) on

The MT6631 combo and everything behind it (btif, irtx, consys) sits on the
MT6358 VCN33 LDO, which nothing in mainline claims: regulator_summary showed
use_count=0 and 3500 mV. Enable it always-on at 3.3 V so the CONN register
window is powered and writable.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index b9f2adff7..4d389bd23 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -735,6 +735,27 @@ &mt6358_vaud28_reg {
 	regulator-always-on;
 };
 
+/*
+ * CONN subsystem rail (VCN33). The MT6631 combo and the CONN peripherals
+ * behind it - btif@1100c000, irtx@1100d000 and the consys window at
+ * 0x18070000 - sit on this LDO; nothing in mainline claims it, and on our boot
+ * the rail stays disabled (regulator_summary: vcn33 use_count=0). With the rail
+ * off those windows still *read* (chip id 0x788, LSR=0x60 come from a stale
+ * path) but every write is dropped: IER/TRI_LVL/THR, the MCR doorbell
+ * (0x1807xx) and APC_CON all read back unchanged. That is exactly the
+ * "BTIF write-dead" wall from docs/STATUS.md 13.11 (4)-(7).
+ *
+ * The vendor kernel enables the rail from its WMT driver through the stock
+ * "vcn33_bt"/"vcn33_wifi" handles. Keep it on: the cost is a few mA and it
+ * makes the whole CONN register window writable.
+ */
+&mt6358_vcn33_reg {
+	regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+	regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+	regulator-always-on;
+	regulator-boot-on;
+};
+
 &mt6358regulator {
 	vsys-ldo1-supply = <&reg_vsys>;
 	vsys-ldo2-supply = <&reg_vsys>;
